  verses: [
    { v: 1, zh: '美名胜过大财； 恩宠强如金银。', en: 'A good name is more desirable than great riches, and loving favor is better than silver and gold.' },
    { v: 2, zh: '富户穷人在世相遇， 都为耶和华所造。', en: 'The rich and the poor have this in common: The LORD is the maker of them all.' },
    { v: 3, zh: '通达人见祸藏躲； 愚蒙人前往受害。', en: 'A prudent man sees danger and hides himself; but the simple pass on, and suffer for it.' },
    { v: 4, zh: '敬畏耶和华心存谦卑， 就得富有、尊荣、生命为赏赐。', en: 'The result of humility and the fear of the LORD is wealth, honor, and life.' },
    { v: 5, zh: '乖僻人的路上有荆棘和网罗； 保守自己生命的，必要远离。', en: 'Thorns and snares are in the path of the wicked; whoever guards his soul stays far from them.' },
    { v: 6, zh: '教养孩童，使他走当行的道， 就是到老他也不偏离。', en: 'Train up a child in the way he should go, and when he is old he will not depart from it.' },
    { v: 7, zh: '富户管辖穷人； 欠债的是债主的仆人。', en: 'The rich rule over the poor. The borrower is servant to the lender.' },
    { v: 8, zh: '撒罪孽的，必收灾祸； 他逞怒的杖也必废掉。', en: 'He who sows wickedness reaps trouble, and the rod of his fury will be destroyed.' },
    { v: 9, zh: '眼目慈善的，就必蒙福， 因他将食物分给穷人。', en: 'He who has a generous eye will be blessed, for he shares his food with the poor.' },
    { v: 10, zh: '赶出亵慢人，争端就消除； 纷争和羞辱也必止息。', en: 'Drive out the mocker, and strife will go out; yes, quarrels and insults will stop.' },
    { v: 11, zh: '喜爱清心的人因他嘴上的恩言， 王必与他为友。', en: 'He who loves purity of heart and speaks gracefully is the king’s friend.' },
    { v: 12, zh: '耶和华的眼目眷顾聪明人， 却倾败奸诈人的言语。', en: 'The LORD’s eyes watch over knowledge, but he frustrates the words of the unfaithful.' },
    { v: 13, zh: '懒惰人说：外头有狮子； 我在街上就必被杀。', en: 'The sluggard says, “There is a lion outside! I will be killed in the streets!”' },
    { v: 14, zh: '淫妇的口为深坑； 耶和华所憎恶的，必陷在其中。', en: 'The mouth of an adulteress is a deep pit. He who is under the LORD’s wrath will fall into it.' },
    { v: 15, zh: '愚蒙迷住孩童的心， 用管教的杖可以远远赶除。', en: 'Folly is bound up in the heart of a child; the rod of discipline drives it far from him.' },
    { v: 16, zh: '欺压贫穷为要利己的， 并送[礼]与富户的，都必缺乏。', en: 'Whoever oppresses the poor for his own increase and whoever gives to the rich, both come to poverty.' },
    { v: 17, zh: '你须侧耳听受智慧人的言语， 留心领会我的知识。', en: 'Turn your ear, and listen to the words of the wise. Apply your heart to my teaching.' },
    { v: 18, zh: '你若心中存记， 嘴上咬定，这便为美。', en: 'For it is a pleasant thing if you keep them within you, if all of them are ready on your lips.' },
    { v: 19, zh: '我今日以此特特指教你， 为要使你倚靠耶和华。', en: 'I teach you today, even you, so that your trust may be in the LORD.' },
    { v: 20, zh: '谋略和知识的美事， 我岂没有写给你吗？', en: 'Haven’t I written to you thirty excellent things of counsel and knowledge,' },
    { v: 21, zh: '要使你知道真言的实理， 你好将真言回复那打发你来的人。', en: 'To teach you truth, reliable words, to give sound answers to the ones who sent you?' },
    { v: 22, zh: '贫穷人，你不可因他贫穷就抢夺他的物， 也不可在城门口欺压困苦人；', en: 'Don’t exploit the poor because he is poor; and don’t crush the needy in court;' },
    { v: 23, zh: '因耶和华必为他辨屈； 抢夺他的，耶和华必夺取那人的命。', en: 'for the LORD will plead their case, and plunder the life of those who plunder them.' },
    { v: 24, zh: '好生气的人，不可与他结交； 暴怒的人，不可与他来往；', en: 'Don’t befriend a hot-tempered man. Don’t associate with one who harbors anger,' },
    { v: 25, zh: '恐怕你效法他的行为， 自己就陷在网罗里。', en: 'lest you learn his ways and ensnare your soul.' },
    { v: 26, zh: '不要与人击掌， 不要为欠债的作保。', en: 'Don’t you be one of those who strike hands, of those who are collateral for debts.' },
    { v: 27, zh: '你若没有什么偿还， 何必使人夺去你睡卧的床呢？', en: 'If you don’t have means to pay, why should he take away your bed from under you?' },
    { v: 28, zh: '你先祖所立的地界， 你不可挪移。', en: 'Don’t move the ancient boundary stone which your fathers have set up.' },
    { v: 29, zh: '你看见办事殷勤的人吗？ 他必站在君王面前， 必不站在下贱人面前。', en: 'Do you see a man skilled in his work? He will serve kings. He won’t serve obscure men.' },
  ],

